[agent]
I got a working Kelta 0.2.0 stack and created a first collection, `quickstart_tasks`, with a required `title` field. I also wrote a record to it and read it back. One part differs from the README: you already have dev servers on ports 5173 and 8080, so I ran Kelta on different ports and did the sign-in and collection steps with curl instead of the browser.

## Commands I ran

| Step | Command | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Clone | `git clone https://github.com/kelta-io/kelta.git && cd kelta` | OK |
| Prerequisites | `docker compose version`, `make --version` | Compose v5.5.1, GNU Make 3.81 |
| Port check | `lsof -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN -P` | **Conflict:** your `<host dev server>` Vite server is on :5173 and your `<host dev server>` node server is on :8080 |
| Setup | `make setup` | OK. It pulled `node:20-alpine` and wrote 5 secrets to `.env` |
| Start | `docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f <scratchpad>/ports.override.yml up -d --wait` | All 9 containers healthy in about 1 minute |
| Step 1: password | `docker compose logs kelta-auth \| grep -o 'Password: *[A-Za-z0-9]*'` | Worked as documented |
| Step 1: sign in | curl through kelta-auth's `/login` and then `/change-password` forms | 302 to `/change-password`, then 302 to `/login?passwordChanged` |
| Token | `POST http://auth.localhost:8081/auth/direct-login` | Got an access token |
| Step 2: create | `POST /default/api/collections`, then `POST /default/api/fields` (the same calls the wizard makes) | 201, 201 |
| Check | `POST`/`GET /default/api/quickstart_tasks`; `GET http://localhost:15173/default/` | Record 201 and read back; UI 200 |

The override file only moved the gateway to 18080 and the UI to 15173. I didn't stop your servers or change anything in the repo.

## What confused me

1. **The ports can't be changed, and the README doesn't say so.** 5173 and 8080 are fixed in `docker-compose.yml`, in the released UI bundle (it calls `http://localhost:8080` directly from the browser), and in the OAuth redirect URI (`http://localhost:5173/auth/callback`). The only fix is to free those ports. The README should list them as a requirement before `docker compose up`.
2. **Don't open the UI on 15173 in a browser right now.** Login would fail, and the UI would send its API calls with your token to your own <host dev server> on :8080. To use the UI, stop your two dev servers, run `docker compose down`, and then run a plain `docker compose up -d --wait`.
3. **The password command prints the label too.** It outputs `Password:  ByZB…`, so you have to copy just the token.
4. **The README doesn't mention that you must change the password on first sign-in.** In a browser that's probably fine, but it's an extra step.
5. **Every API call needs the tenant in the path.** `/api/collections` returns 401 "Tenant context required"; `/default/api/collections` works. The README only mentions this for the UI URL.
6. **The service list is out of date.** The README says `up` starts eight services, but Mailpit starts as well, even though the port table lists it under `--profile tools`.
7. **The UI Dockerfile's default API URL looks wrong.** It defaults `VITE_API_BASE_URL` to `https://api.kelta.io`. The released image is fine (it points at `localhost:8080`), but I had to check that by hand.

## Still running

The stack is still running and the admin password is now the one saved in `<scratchpad>/newpw`. To remove everything, including the volumes, run `docker compose down -v` from `<workdir>/kelta`.

